Synthetic data generated by Generate in this package (seeded PCG), released
under the repository licence. It contains no real telemetry: services, hosts,
tenants and identifiers are invented.

The schema is modelled on the OpenTelemetry trace data model (ResourceSpans,
ScopeSpans, Span, Event, Link, Status, AnyValue), opentelemetry-proto v1.5.0,
Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto/tree/v1.5.0/opentelemetry/proto
Attribute keys follow the OpenTelemetry semantic conventions (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions). No file from either
project is copied; only the message shape and attribute names are reused.

Deviations from OTLP: key-value lists are maps, AnyValue is a record of nullable
branches (no kvlist), timestamps are timestamp-micros because hamba/avro has no
timestamp-nanos, and ids are fixed(16)/fixed(8).

Regenerate sample.jsonl.zst with (the second run checks the embedded copy):

    go test ./datasets/otel -update && go test ./datasets/otel
